speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, I move the adjournment of the House under Standing Order 26 for the purpose of debating a matter of grave concern requiring immediate and urgent consideration, namely:
1.	That several convicted murderers have been sentenced to hang very shortly;
2.	That, in certain defined circumstances, the Governor in Council has power to commute the death penalty;
3.	That the application of this power may be exercised, as in the past decade;

April 30, 1975
Members' Salaries
4.	That the Canadian Police Association and other police associations oppose the commutation of the death penalty, particularly where clemency has not been recommended;
5.	That a recent study in the United States has proven that capital punishment is a deterrent;
6.	That this matter is a grave and urgent matter because the Governor in Council must make a decision on at least one case tomorrow, and others soon.
